literal** — `contains('Me')` is `syntax error, unexpected INVALID_CHARUMENT`. So the
naive "just swap the quote styles" fix does **not** work. Working options, all tested:
1. double quotes inside single quotes (normal habit) — the recommended form;
2. single quotes inside double quotes, escaping as needed;
3. `jq -f filter.jq input.json` — no shell quoting at all, best for long filters;
4. keep the string out of the filter: `jq '.[] | select(.msg | contains($s))' --arg s 'Me'`
(shell quoting is then harmless because there are no quotes inside the filter).

